WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.437
This is a simulated robot installation:
one robot arm at a kitchen table.

2
00:00:05.437 --> 00:00:09.096
Its policy, the model that turns its
camera images,

3
00:00:09.096 --> 00:00:14.033
a written instruction and the hand's
measured pose into motion, is fixed.

4
00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:17.809
Agents watch the installation, run
experiments on it,

5
00:00:17.809 --> 00:00:21.352
and change how the installation uses that
policy.

6
00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:25.158
First story: make this one job.

7
00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:28.723
The robot already has skills.

8
00:00:28.723 --> 00:00:33.988
Each skill is one task on this table, done
by the policy under its own instruction.

9
00:00:33.988 --> 00:00:36.815
Here, each one runs alone and delivers.

10
00:00:36.815 --> 00:00:40.196
The policy does not change anywhere in
this film.

11
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:45.624
A shift lead asks for one job: the cheese
into the black bowl,

12
00:00:45.624 --> 00:00:48.577
and the loaded bowl onto the cabinet top.

13
00:00:48.577 --> 00:00:51.531
The cheese goes in before the bowl moves.

14
00:00:51.531 --> 00:00:56.045
The shift lead's bar: 3 deliveries in
every 5 fresh starts, 12 of 20.

15
00:00:56.045 --> 00:00:59.054
The agent offers to be judged on 14 of 20.

16
00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:05.114
The obvious chain switches to the next
skill the moment the first one reports

17
00:01:05.114 --> 00:01:06.185
success.

18
00:01:06.185 --> 00:01:09.076
That is the signal published scores count.

19
00:01:09.076 --> 00:01:12.555
On the first 10 development starts, it
delivers on 0.

20
00:01:12.555 --> 00:01:15.071
A success signal is not a delivery.

21
00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:21.125
The agent reads the object traces, looks
at the frames, and writes its own check:

22
00:01:21.125 --> 00:01:24.873
was the cheese released and settled when
the bowl task began,

23
00:01:24.873 --> 00:01:27.492
and did it stay in the bowl to the end?

24
00:01:27.492 --> 00:01:30.470
Then it tests transitions on the
installation.

25
00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:35.297
Letting the cheese instruction run on a
little after its goal first holds delivers

26
00:01:35.297 --> 00:01:37.299
on 9 of the same 10 starts.

27
00:01:37.299 --> 00:01:40.585
On 20 fresh starts, the same program
delivers on 11.

28
00:01:40.585 --> 00:01:44.539
Adding a return home at the end breaks
starts that had delivered.

29
00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:50.650
The first shift writes its account to the
shift lead and hands on what it built:

30
00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:53.572
a check that finds where a delivery is
lost,

31
00:01:53.572 --> 00:01:57.016
and a skill on why a return home can break
a delivery.

32
00:01:57.016 --> 00:02:01.243
It took 5 sessions, 100 development
executions on 30 distinct starts,

33
00:02:01.243 --> 00:02:04.008
and 38 minutes of the agent's model time.

34
00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:08.226
The second shift starts from that library.

35
00:02:08.226 --> 00:02:11.695
It runs the first shift's check on its own
baseline,

36
00:02:11.695 --> 00:02:16.301
then builds a sharper one that finds where
the load is lost in transport.

37
00:02:16.301 --> 00:02:21.070
Its longer continuation delivers on 17 of
20 starts it had already examined.

38
00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:25.134
It took 5 sessions, 130 executions on 30
starts and 45 minutes.

39
00:02:25.134 --> 00:02:28.386
The third shift starts from the library of
both.

40
00:02:28.386 --> 00:02:32.505
Its shorter continuation delivers on 9 of
10 development starts,

41
00:02:32.505 --> 00:02:35.810
and the agent saves it as the job, in 5
sessions,

42
00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:38.737
60 executions on 10 starts and 39 minutes.

43
00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:47.065
The saved job runs on the 20 reserved
starts no shift had touched,

44
00:02:47.065 --> 00:02:50.522
and the naive chain runs on the same
starts.

45
00:02:50.522 --> 00:02:54.041
The job delivers on 13; the naive chain on
1.

46
00:02:54.041 --> 00:02:55.523
Rescued: 13.

47
00:02:55.523 --> 00:02:56.881
Broken: 1.

48
00:02:56.881 --> 00:02:58.856
Order violations: 0.

49
00:02:58.856 --> 00:03:02.684
Against the lead's bar of 12, the job is
released.

50
00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:06.934
The robot policy stayed the same.

51
00:03:06.934 --> 00:03:11.808
The installation now runs a released job
it did not have before the first shift:

52
00:03:11.808 --> 00:03:15.570
the cheese in the bowl, and the loaded
bowl on the cabinet.

53
00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:20.285
Behind it, the library holds the job, 4
checks and the skills of every shift.

54
00:03:20.285 --> 00:03:24.576
The second job, the bowl onto the plate,
builds on job one's library.

55
00:03:24.576 --> 00:03:29.503
Its first shift tests job one's checks on
its own first runs and saves a check of

56
00:03:29.503 --> 00:03:30.563
its own;

57
00:03:30.563 --> 00:03:33.530
its second starts from the released
library,

58
00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:37.662
runs job one's audit on its own baseline,
adapts job one's recipe,

59
00:03:37.662 --> 00:03:41.795
and saves a new check and 2 skills from 90
development executions.

60
00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:47.001
Second story: make that a check the next
shift can run.

61
00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:51.518
A fleet of robot arms works at several
sites.

62
00:03:51.518 --> 00:03:55.527
At one site, inference stays in the
customer's data center,

63
00:03:55.527 --> 00:03:59.479
so commands arrive late, and nobody on
site can undo that.

64
00:03:59.479 --> 00:04:04.730
Task telemetry shows a lag there, and a
lag on one robot at another site as well.

65
00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:09.755
From the telemetry alone, the agent cannot
tell what kind of lag each one is.

66
00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:13.448
So the agent builds a measurement.

67
00:04:13.448 --> 00:04:16.941
From a bounded set of motions it composes
a step probe,

68
00:04:16.941 --> 00:04:21.164
and asks for it on a robot at the delayed
site, on the lagging robot,

69
00:04:21.164 --> 00:04:24.709
on a healthy reference and on a robot at
the third site.

70
00:04:24.709 --> 00:04:27.837
Commanded against measured: at the delayed
site,

71
00:04:27.837 --> 00:04:31.069
the arm starts late by the same amount
every time.

72
00:04:31.069 --> 00:04:35.240
On the lagging robot, the delay changes
from one repeat to the next,

73
00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:37.273
and grows within the probe.

74
00:04:37.273 --> 00:04:38.993
One is a fixed delay.

75
00:04:38.993 --> 00:04:40.818
The other is a backlog.

76
00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:46.578
The probe picks candidates; task
experiments on paired starts decide.

77
00:04:46.578 --> 00:04:50.061
The agent adopts its changes, each with
its reason:

78
00:04:50.061 --> 00:04:54.318
compensate for the delay at the first site
rather than remove it,

79
00:04:54.318 --> 00:04:57.635
roll back the software update at the third
site,

80
00:04:57.635 --> 00:05:00.676
and service the lagging robot's
controller.

81
00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:32.343
Then the changed fleet runs 576 reserved
attempts the agent never saw,

82
00:05:32.343 --> 00:05:36.368
beside the original state on the same
attempts.

83
00:05:36.368 --> 00:05:39.028
Before: 451 of 576 succeed.

84
00:05:39.028 --> 00:05:40.597
After: 558.

85
00:05:40.597 --> 00:05:42.303
Rescued: 113.

86
00:05:42.303 --> 00:05:43.803
Broken: 6.

87
00:05:43.803 --> 00:05:47.555
The lagging robot goes from 29 to 46 of
48.

88
00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:53.980
The probe and its analysis became a recipe
in the library, runnable on named robots.

89
00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:57.668
On a later fleet, robots fail again, and
the recipe runs.

90
00:05:57.668 --> 00:05:59.271
At the third site,

91
00:05:59.271 --> 00:06:04.188
the arms first move 18 rows after the
command and are half-way 21 rows after it:

92
00:06:04.188 --> 00:06:05.577
a fixed delay.

93
00:06:05.577 --> 00:06:09.853
The robot that fails on its own responds
like the healthy reference.

94
00:06:09.853 --> 00:06:14.876
Its first movement comes 1 row after the
command; the reference's, 1 row after it.

95
00:06:14.876 --> 00:06:17.709
So the skill's rule points at the images,

96
00:06:17.709 --> 00:06:21.396
not at the controller service that fixed
the first fleet.

97
00:06:21.396 --> 00:06:25.832
The operator's recorded decision follows
it: no service for that robot;

98
00:06:25.832 --> 00:06:28.504
inspect its images and its change log,

99
00:06:28.504 --> 00:06:33.154
and test the first fleet's adaptation at
the third site before adopting it.

100
00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:36.958
Every clip in this film is a recorded run.

101
00:06:36.958 --> 00:06:38.722
The record lists each one.
